A reliable Azure network architecture provides connectivity between applications, users, Azure services, and on-premises infrastructure while maintaining appropriate security boundaries.

Important networking components include:

* Virtual Networks
* Subnets
* Network Security Groups
* Route tables
* VPN Gateway
* ExpressRoute
* Private connectivity
* Load balancing

For example, a three-tier application may place web servers in one subnet, application servers in another, and databases in a separate subnet with controlled communication between each layer.

A real-life use case is an enterprise extending its existing datacenter into Azure while maintaining secure connectivity between on-premises applications and cloud workloads.

A well-designed network foundation improves security, performance, scalability, and connectivity.
